{"arrivo":"de","origine":"dum","origine_nome":"Middle Dutch","livello2":"la-med","livello2_nome":"Medieval Latin","n":1,"parole":[{"parola":"Almanach","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Of uncertain origin; Probably; perhaps","significato":"almanac, yearbook","termine_origine":"almanag","catena":[{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"almanag","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"almanach","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"},{"codice":"xaa","nome":"Andalusian Arabic","termine":"الْمَنَاخ","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gkm","nome":"Byzantine Greek","termine":"ἀλμενιχιακά","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gkm","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"First attested in the 16th century. Borrowed from Middle Dutch almanag (Flanders 1426), from Medieval Latin almanach (1267), from Andalusian Arabic الْمَنَاخ (al-manāḵ, “calendar”). The Ibero-Arabic term is of uncertain origin. See also almanaque. Perhaps originally derived from Byzantine Greek ἀλμε"}]}